1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,417
We crashed a spacecraft into an asteroid.

2
00:00:02,417 --> 00:00:04,075
Now we're checking the damage.

3
00:00:04,583 --> 00:00:10,319
In 2022, NASA's DART probe hit Dimorphos, a little asteroid moon, on purpose.

4
00:00:10,817 --> 00:00:11,378
It worked.

5
00:00:11,378 --> 00:00:15,474
Its orbit around its bigger partner got about thirty-two minutes shorter.

6
00:00:15,983 --> 00:00:19,451
This month, Europe's Hera spacecraft arrived at the crime scene.

7
00:00:19,950 --> 00:00:23,652
Gravity here is two hundred thousand times weaker than Earth's.

8
00:00:23,652 --> 00:00:26,531
Hera creeps along at twelve centimeters a second.

9
00:00:27,017 --> 00:00:29,223
Like and subscribe for more space news.

10
00:00:29,523 --> 00:00:33,053
Hera will weigh Dimorphos, and see if DART left a crater,

11
00:00:33,053 --> 00:00:34,974
or reshaped the whole asteroid.

12
00:00:35,483 --> 00:00:38,346
Two shoebox-sized CubeSats will fly closer.

13
00:00:38,346 --> 00:00:40,476
One carries radar to see inside.

14
00:00:40,983 --> 00:00:41,875
Still unknown:

15
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:43,849
what the crash site looks like.

16
00:00:43,849 --> 00:00:46,141
First close-ups are due November 25.

17
00:00:46,650 --> 00:00:49,834
It's practice for the day a real asteroid heads our way.

18
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:52,242
Now, what if you lived on Mercury?

19
00:00:52,242 --> 00:00:53,688
Full story on the channel.
